# Template: simulate a powerlaw + blurred-reflection spectrum with fakeit,
# then recover the lamppost height with a fit.
#
# Parameter numbering: powerlaw 1-2; gradus_lamp_thin 3 spin, 4 inc, 5 h,
# 6-10 xillver, 11 redshift, 12 norm.
#
# Notes:
# - fakeit prompt order can differ slightly between XSPEC versions; adjust the
#   inline answers (y / file name / exposure) if yours differs.
# - The fit steps h across its 0.25 r_g grid; each new grid corner costs one
#   ray-traced kernel on the first fit and is cached on disk afterwards.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   xspec - examples/xspec/fake_and_fit.xcm
lmod gradusxspec .
dummyrsp 0.5 10.0 300 log
model powerlaw + gradus_lamp_thin & 2.0 & 1.0 & /*
# Freeze everything in the reflection component except the lamppost height.
freeze 3-11
thaw 5
# Simulate at the "true" height h = 5 r_g.
newpar 5 5.0
fakeit none & y & & fake_lamp.fak & 50000, 1.0, 50000
ignore **-0.5 10.0-**
# Displace the height and let the fit pull it back.
newpar 5 8.0
fit 100
show parameters
